 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to including reproductive\nhealth conditions that affect female fertility as part of the health care and\nwellness education and outreach program",
    "basePrintNo": "S6957",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6957-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §207, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6957\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to including repro-\nductive health conditions that affect female fertility as part of the\nhealth care and wellness education and outreach program\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo increase public awareness on reproductive health conditions that\naffect female fertility.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would amend the public health law to authorize the Commission-\ner of Health to conduct an education and outreach program for consumers,\npatients, educators, and health care providers relating to reproductive\nhealth conditions that affect female fertility.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAccording to the US Department of Health and Human Services, Polycystic\nOvarian Syndrome (PCOS) is the most common cause of female infertility\naffecting 1 in 10 women, which is over 6.1 million women nationally. As\nthe rates of female infertility are increasing, we must increase public\nawareness to equip those at risk so they may be able to seek appropriate\nmedical treatment.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: A8702 - Referred to Health\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
